EXT. THE GLASS BRIDGE OF AETHERMERE - DAWN

A span of living crystal between two floating islands, fog beneath it, bells ringing somewhere unseen.

QUEEN IDRISSA, tall and crowned in silver thorns, stands at the middle of the bridge. Behind her, SIR BALTHAZAR, white-bearded, in bronze plate, grips a staff that hums with blue light. Before her, a ragged young WANDERER named FINNEGAN carries nothing but a cracked lute.

IDRISSA
You trespass, minstrel.

FINNEGAN
I'm only crossing.

BALTHAZAR
Cross to what?

FINNEGAN
To the far island. My brother's there.

IDRISSA
There is no brother.

BALTHAZAR ^
There is no brother.

A third figure strides out of the fog: MORGANA, a woman in green, hair full of leaves, a bow slung across her back. She holds up a hand.

MORGANA
Lower your staff, Balthazar. He speaks true.

BALTHAZAR
How would you know?

MORGANA
Because the brother is me.

Finnegan drops the lute. It rings on the crystal. The bridge begins to hum.
